@page "/chart-large-data"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Radzen Blazor Chart with Large Data
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    A line with hundreds of thousands of points has far more points than the chart has pixels. Set <code>Sampling</code> to <code>Sampling.MinMax</code> and the series keeps only the first, the lowest, the highest and the last point of every half pixel - at most eight points per pixel - so the line keeps its shape and its peaks while the chart stays fast.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="Chart" Example="ChartLargeDataConfig">
    <ChartLargeDataConfig />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-8">
    How it works
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Sampling only changes what is drawn. Tooltips and clicks still use every point, and zooming in brings back the detail: once the visible points are fewer than the pixels, all of them are drawn again.
    Raise <code>MaxZoom</code> so the mouse wheel can zoom far enough to reach the individual points.
    Sampling is available for line and area series and is skipped when <code>AnimateDataUpdates</code> is enabled.
    A sampled series reads its data once and remembers its range. Assigning a new collection to <code>Data</code> is picked up automatically; after changing items in place call <code>Reload()</code> on the chart.
</RadzenText>
